min-for-convenience wildcard IAM grant or commits a plaintext secret and T10 stays silent because the resource is 'transient'"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Broaden the safety qualifier to preserve all four MAJOR classes on transient infra, e.g. 'This exclusion does NOT waive the MAJOR safety classes: a transient service still owes b2 endpoint auth if untrusted-network-reachable, and a transient apply that destroys shared/stateful data, grants wildcard admin, or commits a plaintext secret is still in scope — flag it.' If the narrower waiver is intentional, say so explicitly and add a must-not-fire dataset case pinning that a destructive/secret-leaking transient experiment is deliberately out of scope.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add `plan-review-T10` to the `NEW_SPECS` tuple in tests/unit/test_new_eval_specs.py (or otherwise wire the new packaged spec into a strict-validation test named in the Testing step) so AC5's strict-validation and dataset-balance checks actually run against it.","cohort